<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name      "unraid.themer">
  <!ENTITY author    "benjaminmue">
  <!ENTITY version   "2026.07.25.2">
  <!ENTITY launch    "Settings/UnraidThemer">
  <!ENTITY pluginURL "https://github.com/benjaminmue/unraid-themer/raw/refs/heads/main/unraid-themer.plg">
  <!ENTITY support   "https://github.com/benjaminmue/unraid-themer">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="&support;" min="7.0.0" icon="paint-brush">

<CHANGES>
## Unraid Themer
## 2026.07.25.2
- New "SpongeBob" icon set — an under-the-sea joke set: Docker becomes a whale,
  the dashboard a pineapple, the fan a starfish, CPU a coral, users a jellyfish,
  shares a treasure chest, and so on. Sea motifs from game-icons.net (CC BY 3.0);
  slots without a sea equivalent fall back to Lucide. Pairs with the SpongeBob
  store theme. Pick it under "Icon set".

## 2026.07.25.1
- Fix the Custom Icons page showing its JavaScript as raw text: Unraid runs the
  page through markdown, which split the multi-line inline script on its blank
  lines. Moved the page JS to an external file (js/themer-icons.js); config is
  passed via data-* attributes. The icon grid picker works again.

## 2026.07.25
- Fix updates not being offered: PHP version_compare() treats letter suffixes
  like "z"/"aa"/"ab" as equal, so the update check never saw them as newer.
  Switched to a numeric date scheme (2026.07.25, then .1, .2, ...) that always
  compares correctly. Contains everything from 24aa/24ab.
- Fix nginx error-log spam: the header bell/menu swap tried a non-existent
  per-set path (icons/svg/lucide/bell.svg) before falling back; it now loads the
  flat icon directly, with in-flight de-duplication.

## 2026.07.24ab
- Five more bundled icon sets: Iconoir, Remix, Bootstrap, Carbon and Material
  Symbols (fetched via the Iconify API in the generator, missing glyphs fall
  back to Lucide). Nine sets total now — all appear in the "Icon set" dropdown
  and, grouped, in the per-slot grid picker. The picker discovers sets
  automatically from the bundled folders.

## 2026.07.24aa
- Custom Icons: the grid picker now shows ALL bundled sets (Lucide, Tabler,
  Phosphor, Heroicons), grouped and searchable — pick e.g. "tabler/cpu" for any
  slot. The main settings page gets a prominent "Open Themer Icons" button.

## 2026.07.24z
- Sidebar polish (Azure / Gray): the top header band now matches the content
  background (was a lighter gray), and the active/hover nav item uses a subtle
  preset-aware accent (flat tint + left accent bar) instead of the stock loud
  red-orange gradient. Preset-agnostic layout.css, no-op on top-nav layouts.

## 2026.07.24y
- Sidebar layouts (Azure / Gray) supported: the base pairing now keeps your
  layout family — on Azure/Gray a dark preset pairs to Gray and a light one to
  Azure, instead of switching you to the top-nav Black/White. bebamu's dark
  rules now also apply on the Gray base. (Azure/Gray share the same CSS
  variables as White/Black, so preset colors already carry over.)

## 2026.07.24x
- Custom Icons page: the per-row grid + upload buttons now show their glyphs
  (were blank on Unraid's button styling) — styled as subtle icon buttons.
- Header swap keeps the original icon's sizing class, so swapped bell/menu
  icons always render at the right size.

## 2026.07.24w
- Header bell/menu swap is more robust: the Vue header mounts async from ES
  modules, so retry over a longer window and on DOM mutations until both the
  notifications bell and the account menu are swapped, then stop.

## 2026.07.24v
- Header toolbar now themed properly: the bottom row (search, logout, terminal,
  file manager, feedback, info, log, help, language) uses Unraid's own icon font
  (icon-u-*) and is now mapped by the CSS icon set like everything else.
- The top-right notifications bell and account dropdown (Vue inline SVGs) are
  matched more reliably (accessible name incl. sr-only text) and swapped via JS.

## 2026.07.24u
- Header icons: best-effort swap of the whole Vue-header toolbar (search, logout,
  terminal, clone, feedback, remote, notifications bell, menu, help, ...) — which
  lives in an open shadow DOM unreachable by CSS — to match the active icon set,
  via a defensive shadow-DOM pass in themer.js. Only runs with an icon set active,
  matches buttons by their accessible name, and only replaces the SVG visual —
  no-ops on any miss, never touches handlers.

## 2026.07.24t
- Icon sets: three more bundled open-source sets — Tabler, Phosphor, Heroicons
  (in addition to Lucide). Pick one under "Icon set". Missing glyphs in a set
  fall back to Lucide so a set is always complete.
- Custom Icons: upload your own SVG file per slot (validated like pasted markup),
  next to the grid picker.

## 2026.07.24s
- Custom Icons: pick icons from a visual, searchable grid (like an emoji picker,
  but the actual Lucide icons) instead of a text-only dropdown. Each row has a
  "pick" button that opens the grid; the text field still accepts a name, https
  SVG URL or pasted SVG for anything custom.

## 2026.07.24r
- Custom Icons is now its own entry under Settings > Utilities ("Themer Icons")
  — the sub-tab under the main page did not render. The two pages cross-link.

## 2026.07.24q
- Custom Icons: new sub-page (Settings > Utilities > Unraid Themer > Custom
  Icons) listing every themeable icon slot with its reference icon and a live
  preview. Assign a custom icon per slot — a bundled Lucide name, a raw https
  SVG URL, or pasted SVG markup. Inputs are validated (no scripts, event
  handlers or external refs), stored on flash, and compiled into overrides.css
  that wins over the icon set (works even with set = Default).

## 2026.07.24p
- Icon set (Lucide): remap the remaining Docker-menu action glyphs — WebUI /
  Project Page (globe), Edit (wrench), Support (life-ring), Logs (list) and
  help — so the container context menu is fully Lucide.

## 2026.07.24o
- Icon set (Lucide): also swaps the Font Awesome action glyphs used on the
  Docker / VM / tile toolbars (play, stop, pause, restart, power, cog, trash,
  terminal, download, chevrons, ...) so the whole UI uses one line-icon set.

## 2026.07.24n
- Icon set (v1): optional "Lucide" set swaps Unraid's UI glyphs (docker, cpu,
  disks, fan, ...) for open-source line icons that tint with the theme, via
  CSS mask. Pick it under "Icon set"; "Default" keeps Unraid's icons.

## 2026.07.24m
- Only bebamu is now built-in; the other default themes are seeded to flash on
  first install, so they can be uninstalled from the store like any added theme
  (and stay removed).

## 2026.07.24l
- Store: user-added themes now show an "Uninstall" button (built-in stay
  "Installed"). The separate "Added themes" row now only lists URL imports
  that aren't in the store.

## 2026.07.24k
- Move the "Added themes" (remove) section down next to the theme store, so
  all theme management is grouped together.

## 2026.07.24j
- Fix layout: "Added themes" remove buttons no longer span full width; the
  theme store list now stays in the form column instead of breaking left.

## 2026.07.24i
- Remove themes you added: imported / store themes show under "Added themes"
  with a remove button (built-in presets stay).

## 2026.07.24h
- Added 4 light themes (Catppuccin Latte, Solarized Light, Rose Pine Dawn,
  GitHub Light) — bundled and in the store.
- Store browser: search box + Light/Dark filter + scrollable list (scales to
  many themes).
- Preset help now notes the base is auto-paired on Apply.

## 2026.07.24g
- Store browser now uses a non-CDN-cached URL so newly published themes appear
  immediately (added Catppuccin Mocha to the registry).

## 2026.07.24f
- Theme store (mode B): browse the community registry in the settings page and
  download themes on demand (validated before saving). Already-installed themes
  are marked. Backed by a GitHub Action that sanitises every submitted theme.

## 2026.07.24e
- Theme store (mode A): import a community theme from a raw .css URL. The CSS
  is validated (scripts, javascript:, @import and external url() rejected)
  before it is saved and added to the preset dropdown.

## 2026.07.24d
- Auto-pair the base theme: selecting a dark preset now switches the Dynamix
  base to Black on Apply (via Unraid's own config writer) so the Vue
  web-components (notifications panel) and Community Apps render dark too.

## 2026.07.24c
- Plugins list: restore the plugin title (use a bold first line, not an H1).

## 2026.07.24b
- CRITICAL: loader no longer leaks PHP globals ($name etc.) — this broke
  navigation to Share / Disk / Device settings pages (they use a global $name).
  The loader now runs inside an isolated closure.
- Plugins page: removed the README heading that rendered the name oversized.

## 2026.07.24a
- Dark presets: fix light table rows, Community Apps cards and "white bars"
  (remap Dynamix tablesorter + CA variables to the preset's own colors).
- Dashboard CPU/Net charts: theme-neutral grid + themed labels (was harsh on dark).
- Settings: guidance to use the Black base theme with dark presets.

## 2026.07.24
- Initial scaffold.
- Buttons-loader injection (enabled/disabled), preset dropdown, custom CSS overrides.
- Presets: bebamu (Light/Dark), Nord, Dracula, Solarized Dark, Monokai, Gruvbox Dark.
- Runtime JS: Docker "update available" badge + tooltip, shadow-DOM style bridge.
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
# --- Unraid Themer: prepare directories ---
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/presets /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/js /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/defaults /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/overrides
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/unraid.themer/presets /boot/config/plugins/unraid.themer/overrides
exit 0
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/README.md">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[**Unraid Themer**

A generic theming plugin for the Unraid 7 webGUI. Pick a preset (or drop your own
CSS), toggle it on/off, and the whole UI restyles — classic Dynamix pages and the
new Vue web-components, via CSS custom properties.

Open **Settings → Utilities → Unraid Themer**.

Presets: bebamu (Light + Dark), Nord, Dracula, Solarized Dark, Monokai, Gruvbox Dark.
Custom CSS overrides load on top of the preset. Semantic status colors (disk health,
array state) are left untouched. Zero footprint when disabled.

Add your own preset by dropping `<name>.css` in
`/boot/config/plugins/unraid.themer/presets/`.
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/UnraidThemer.page">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[Menu="Utilities"
Title="Unraid Themer"
Icon="paint-brush"
---
<?php
/* Unraid Themer — settings page (Settings → Utilities → Unraid Themer).
 * Lets the user enable the theme, pick a preset, and add custom CSS overrides.
 * Source of truth is flash (/boot/config/plugins/unraid.themer); files are
 * mirrored to the RAM webroot so nginx can serve them.
 */
require_once "$docroot/plugins/dynamix/include/Wrappers.php";

/* Validate imported CSS before we ever write it to disk. Returns [clean, error].
 * This is the security core of the theme store: reject anything that could run
 * code or phone home. Same ruleset the future publish-bot will use. */
function themer_sanitize_css($css) {
    $css = (string) $css;
    if (trim($css) === '')        return ["", "empty or download failed"];
    if (strlen($css) > 512 * 1024) return ["", "file too large (>512 KB)"];
    $blocked = [
        '/<\s*script/i'                          => "contains a <script> tag",
        '/<\s*\/?\s*(iframe|object|embed|base)/i' => "contains embedded HTML",
        '/javascript\s*:/i'                      => "contains a javascript: URI",
        '/expression\s*\(/i'                     => "contains a CSS expression()",
        '/behaviou?r\s*:/i'                      => "contains a CSS behavior:",
        '/-moz-binding/i'                        => "contains -moz-binding",
        '/@import/i'                             => "contains @import",
        '/url\s*\(\s*[\'"]?\s*(https?:|\/\/)/i'  => "loads an external url()",
    ];
    foreach ($blocked as $re => $why) {
        if (preg_match($re, $css)) return ["", $why];
    }
    return [$css, ""];
}

$name        = "unraid.themer";
$flash       = "/boot/config/plugins/$name";
$webroot     = "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$name";
$cfg_path    = "$flash/$name.cfg";
$custom_flash= "$flash/custom.css";
$custom_web  = "$webroot/custom.css";
// github.com/.../raw/ serves fresh content immediately; raw.githubusercontent
// is CDN-cached (~5 min), so new store themes would appear late.
$store_base  = "https://github.com/benjaminmue/unraid-themer/raw/refs/heads/main/themes";
$msg = "";
$switch_base = "";   // set to a theme name if we need to pair the Dynamix base

// download + sanitise a theme into the presets folder; returns "" or an error
function themer_fetch_theme($url, $flash, $webroot) {
    $raw = shell_exec("curl -fsSL --max-time 20 --max-filesize 524288 " . escapeshellarg($url) . " 2>/dev/null");
    [$clean, $err] = themer_sanitize_css($raw);
    if ($err) return $err;
    $stem = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9_-]/', '', strtolower(pathinfo((string) parse_url($url, PHP_URL_PATH), PATHINFO_FILENAME)));
    if ($stem === '' || $stem === 'none') $stem = 'imported';
    @mkdir("$flash/presets", 0755, true);
    file_put_contents("$flash/presets/$stem.css", $clean);
    @copy("$flash/presets/$stem.css", "$webroot/presets/$stem.css");
    return "";  // success
}

// --- SAVE ---
if ($_POST && isset($_POST['SAVE_CONFIG'])) {
    $service = ($_POST['SERVICE'] ?? "disabled") === "enabled" ? "enabled" : "disabled";
    $preset  = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/', '', $_POST['PRESET'] ?? 'bebamu');
    if ($preset === '') $preset = 'none';
    $iconset = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/', '', $_POST['ICONSET'] ?? 'default');
    if ($iconset === '') $iconset = 'default';
    @mkdir($flash, 0755, true);
    file_put_contents($cfg_path, "SERVICE=\"$service\"\nPRESET=\"$preset\"\nICONSET=\"$iconset\"\n");

    if (isset($_POST['custom_css'])) {
        // normalise newlines, store on flash, mirror to webroot
        $css = str_replace("\r\n", "\n", $_POST['custom_css']);
        file_put_contents($custom_flash, $css);
        @copy($custom_flash, $custom_web);
    }

    // Auto-pair the base theme: the Vue web-components (notifications, etc.) and
    // Community Apps render light/dark by the BASE Dynamix theme, not by us. A
    // preset can declare `themer-base: black|white`; if the base doesn't match,
    // switch it via Unraid's own canonical writer below.
    $sel_file = "$webroot/presets/$preset.css";
    if ($service === "enabled" && is_file($sel_file)
        && preg_match('/themer-base:\s*(black|white|azure|gray)/i', file_get_contents($sel_file), $m)) {
        // The marker states the wanted MODE (dark = black/gray, light = white/azure).
        // Keep the user's layout family: sidebar bases (azure/gray) pair within
        // sidebar, top-nav bases (white/black) pair within top-nav — so a sidebar
        // user isn't yanked into the top-nav layout just by picking a preset.
        $want = strtolower($m[1]);
        $mode = in_array($want, ['black', 'gray']) ? 'dark' : 'light';
        $cur  = @parse_ini_file('/boot/config/plugins/dynamix/dynamix.cfg', true)['display']['theme'] ?? 'white';
        $sidebar = in_array($cur, ['azure', 'gray']);
        $target = $mode === 'dark' ? ($sidebar ? 'gray' : 'black') : ($sidebar ? 'azure' : 'white');
        if ($target !== $cur) $switch_base = $target;
    }

    $msg = $switch_base
        ? "Settings saved. Switching the base theme to \"" . ucfirst($switch_base) . "\" and reloading…"
        : "Settings saved. Reload the browser (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+R) to see changes.";
}

// --- IMPORT A THEME FROM A URL (theme store, mode A) ---
if ($_POST && isset($_POST['IMPORT_URL'])) {
    $url = trim($_POST['import_url'] ?? '');
    if (!preg_match('#^https://[^\s\'"<>]+\.css([?\#].*)?$#i', $url)) {
        $msg = "Enter an https:// URL that ends in .css";
    } else {
        $err = themer_fetch_theme($url, $flash, $webroot);
        $msg = $err ? "Import rejected — $err." : "Imported. Pick it in the preset dropdown above and click Apply.";
    }
}

// --- GET A THEME FROM THE STORE (theme store, mode B) ---
if ($_POST && isset($_POST['store_get'])) {
    $file = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]/', '', $_POST['store_get']);
    if ($file !== '' && substr($file, -4) === '.css') {
        $err = themer_fetch_theme("$store_base/$file", $flash, $webroot);
        $msg = $err
            ? "Store download rejected — $err."
            : "Added \"" . pathinfo($file, PATHINFO_FILENAME) . "\" from the store. Pick it in the dropdown and Apply.";
    }
}

// --- REMOVE A USER-ADDED THEME ---
if ($_POST && isset($_POST['remove_preset'])) {
    $r = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/', '', $_POST['remove_preset']);
    // only files that live on flash are user-added (bundled presets are recreated
    // from the .plg on boot, so removing them would be pointless)
    if ($r !== '' && is_file("$flash/presets/$r.css")) {
        @unlink("$flash/presets/$r.css");
        @unlink("$webroot/presets/$r.css");
        // if it was the active preset, fall back to bebamu
        $cur = parse_plugin_cfg($name);
        if (($cur['PRESET'] ?? '') === $r) {
            $svc = $cur['SERVICE'] ?? 'disabled';
            $ico = $cur['ICONSET'] ?? 'default';
            file_put_contents($cfg_path, "SERVICE=\"$svc\"\nPRESET=\"bebamu\"\nICONSET=\"$ico\"\n");
        }
        $msg = "Removed \"$r\".";
    }
}

// --- INIT / READ ---
if (!file_exists($custom_flash)) {
    @mkdir($flash, 0755, true);
    file_put_contents($custom_flash, "/* Your custom CSS overrides — loaded on top of the selected preset. */\n");
    @copy($custom_flash, $custom_web);
}
$settings    = parse_plugin_cfg($name);
$service     = $settings['SERVICE'] ?? "disabled";
$preset_sel  = $settings['PRESET']  ?? "bebamu";
$iconset_sel = $settings['ICONSET'] ?? "default";
$custom_css  = file_exists($custom_flash) ? file_get_contents($custom_flash) : "";

// available icon sets (default + any bundled icons/*.css)
$iconsets = ['default'];
foreach (glob("$webroot/icons/*.css") as $ic) $iconsets[] = basename($ic, '.css');

// discover presets shipped in the webroot
$presets = [];
foreach (glob("$webroot/presets/*.css") as $p) $presets[] = basename($p, '.css');
sort($presets);
$have_preset = array_flip($presets);

// user-added themes live on flash (bundled ones are recreated from the .plg) → removable
$user_presets = [];
foreach (glob("$flash/presets/*.css") as $p) $user_presets[] = basename($p, '.css');
sort($user_presets);

// fetch the community theme store index (best-effort, short timeout)
$store_index = null;
$raw = shell_exec("curl -fsSL --connect-timeout 4 --max-time 8 " . escapeshellarg("$store_base/index.json") . " 2>/dev/null");
if ($raw) $store_index = @json_decode($raw, true);

// Build the "Added themes" and "Theme store" blocks as HTML strings, echoed
// inline in the form so Unraid's markdown parser keeps them in the value column.
$btn = 'display:inline-block; width:auto; padding:2px 12px; min-width:88px;';

// theme store rows — three button states: Get / Uninstall (user-added) / Installed (built-in)
$store_stems = [];
if (!empty($store_index['themes'])) {
    $rows = "";
    foreach ($store_index['themes'] as $t) {
        $stem = pathinfo($t['file'], PATHINFO_FILENAME);
        $store_stems[$stem] = 1;
        $ins     = isset($have_preset[$stem]);
        $onflash = is_file("$flash/presets/$stem.css");   // present on flash → user-added → removable
        $base = strtolower($t['base'] ?? '');
        $L = in_array($base, ['white', 'azure', 'any']) ? '1' : '0';
        $D = in_array($base, ['black', 'gray', 'any']) ? '1' : '0';
        $dn = htmlspecialchars(strtolower($t['name'] . ' ' . $t['description']));
        if (!$ins) {
            $b = "<button type='submit' name='store_get' value='" . htmlspecialchars($t['file']) . "' style='$btn'>Get</button>";
        } elseif ($onflash) {
            $b = "<button type='submit' name='remove_preset' value='$stem' onclick='return confirm(\"Uninstall $stem?\")' style='$btn'>Uninstall</button>";
        } else {
            $b = "<button type='button' disabled style='$btn'>Installed</button>";
        }
        $rows .= "<div class='ut-store-row' data-name='$dn' data-light='$L' data-dark='$D' style='display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:10px; padding:6px 8px; border-top:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.18);'>"
            . $b
            . "<span><strong>" . htmlspecialchars($t['name']) . "</strong> &mdash; " . htmlspecialchars($t['description']) . " <em style='opacity:.6;'>(" . htmlspecialchars($t['base']) . " &middot; " . htmlspecialchars($t['author']) . ")</em></span>"
            . "</div>";
    }
    $n = count($store_index['themes']);
    $storeHtml = "<div style='max-width:660px;'>"
        . "<div style='display:flex; gap:8px; margin-bottom:8px; align-items:center;'><input type='text' id='ut-store-search' placeholder='Search themes…' autocomplete='off' onkeyup='utStoreFilter()' style='flex:1; min-width:0;'><select id='ut-store-filter' onchange='utStoreFilter()' style='width:auto;'><option value='all'>All</option><option value='light'>Light</option><option value='dark'>Dark</option></select></div>"
        . "<div id='ut-store-list' style='max-height:320px; overflow-y:auto; border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.25);'>$rows</div>"
        . "<span>$n community themes from the <a href='https://github.com/benjaminmue/unraid-themer/tree/main/themes' target='_blank'>registry</a> &mdash; downloaded on demand and validated before saving.</span>"
        . "</div>"
        . "<script>function utStoreFilter(){var q=(document.getElementById('ut-store-search').value||'').toLowerCase().trim();var f=document.getElementById('ut-store-filter').value;var rows=document.querySelectorAll('#ut-store-list .ut-store-row');for(var i=0;i<rows.length;i++){var r=rows[i];var okq=!q||r.getAttribute('data-name').indexOf(q)>=0;var okf=f=='all'||(f=='light'&&r.getAttribute('data-light')=='1')||(f=='dark'&&r.getAttribute('data-dark')=='1');r.style.display=(okq&&okf)?'':'none';}}</script>";
} else {
    $storeHtml = "<span>Store unavailable (no internet, or GitHub unreachable). The URL import above still works.</span>";
}

// "Added themes" now only covers user imports that AREN'T in the registry
// (arbitrary URL imports); registry themes are removed via "Uninstall" in the store.
$orphans = array_values(array_diff($user_presets, array_keys($store_stems)));
if ($orphans) {
    $addedHtml = "";
    foreach ($orphans as $up) {
        $lbl = htmlspecialchars(ucwords(str_replace(['-', '_'], ' ', $up)));
        $val = htmlspecialchars($up);
        $addedHtml .= "<button type='submit' name='remove_preset' value='$val' onclick='return confirm(\"Remove $val?\")' style='$btn margin:0 6px 6px 0;'>$lbl &times;</button>";
    }
    $addedHtml .= "<br><span>Themes you imported by URL that aren't in the store. Click to remove.</span>";
} else {
    $addedHtml = "<span>Store themes are removed with <strong>Uninstall</strong> in the store above; built-in themes stay.</span>";
}
?>

<div markdown="1">
<?php if ($msg): ?>
<span class="green"><?= htmlspecialchars($msg) ?></span>
<?php endif; ?>
</div>

<?php if ($switch_base): ?>
<script>
// Pair the Dynamix base theme with the selected preset, using Unraid's own
// config writer (csrf is auto-appended by the global ajaxPrefilter), then reload.
$(function () {
  $.post('/update.php', {
    '#file': 'dynamix/dynamix.cfg',
    '#section': 'display',
    'theme': '<?= $switch_base ?>'
  }).always(function () { setTimeout(function () { location.reload(); }, 600); });
});
</script>
<?php endif; ?>

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/Settings/UnraidThemer">

Enable Unraid Themer:
: <select name="SERVICE" size="1">
    <?= mk_option($service, "enabled", "Yes") ?>
    <?= mk_option($service, "disabled", "No") ?>
  </select>
  <span>When disabled, the webGUI is 100% stock — nothing is injected.</span>

Theme preset:
: <select name="PRESET" size="1">
    <?php foreach ($presets as $p): ?>
    <?= mk_option($preset_sel, $p, ucwords(str_replace(['-','_'],' ',$p))) ?>
    <?php endforeach; ?>
    <?= mk_option($preset_sel, "none", "None (custom CSS only)") ?>
  </select>
  <span>Applies on top of the Dynamix base theme. On <strong>Apply</strong> the base is paired automatically: dark presets switch it to <a href="/Settings/DisplaySettings" target="_blank">Black</a>, light presets to White — so tables, Community Apps and the Vue components render in the right mode with no manual step. "bebamu" is base-neutral (White = Light, Black = Dark). Sidebar layouts are supported too — if you're on <strong>Azure</strong>/<strong>Gray</strong>, the pairing stays in the sidebar layout (dark = Gray, light = Azure) instead of switching you to top-nav.</span>

Icon set:
: <select name="ICONSET" size="1">
    <?php foreach ($iconsets as $is): ?>
    <?= mk_option($iconset_sel, $is, ucfirst($is)) ?>
    <?php endforeach; ?>
  </select>
  <span>Swaps Unraid's UI glyphs (Docker, CPU, disks, fan…) for an icon set that tints with the theme. Bundled open-source line sets: <strong>Lucide</strong>, <strong>Tabler</strong>, <strong>Phosphor</strong>, <strong>Heroicons</strong>, <strong>Iconoir</strong>, <strong>Remix</strong>, <strong>Bootstrap</strong>, <strong>Carbon</strong>, <strong>Material Symbols</strong>; <strong>Default</strong> keeps Unraid's own icons. Fine-tune or upload single icons on the <a href="/Settings/UnraidThemerIcons"><strong>Themer Icons</strong></a> page.</span>

Custom icons (per slot):
: <input type="button" value="Open Themer Icons →" onclick="location.href='/Settings/UnraidThemerIcons'" style="font-weight:bold;">
  <span>Assign or upload a custom icon for any individual glyph — pick from all bundled sets or your own SVG.</span>

Custom CSS overrides:
: <textarea name="custom_css" spellcheck="false" style="font-family:monospace; width:100%; max-width:820px; height:45vh; background:#111; color:#eee; border:1px solid #444; padding:10px;"><?= htmlspecialchars($custom_css) ?></textarea>
  <span>Optional. Loaded <em>after</em> the preset, so these rules win. Use Unraid CSS variables, e.g. <code>:root { --background-color:#101010; }</code>.</span>

Import a theme (URL):
: <input type="text" name="import_url" spellcheck="false" placeholder="https://…/theme.css" style="width:100%; max-width:560px;">
  <input type="submit" name="IMPORT_URL" value="Import">
  <span>Paste a raw <code>.css</code> URL (e.g. from GitHub) to add a community theme. It is downloaded, <strong>validated</strong> (scripts, <code>javascript:</code>, <code>@import</code> and external <code>url()</code> are rejected) and added to the preset dropdown.</span>

Theme store:
: <?= $storeHtml ?>

Added themes:
: <?= $addedHtml ?>

&nbsp;
: <span class="buttons-spaced">
    <input type="submit" name="SAVE_CONFIG" value="_(Apply)_">
    <input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
  </span>

&nbsp;
: <span class="description" style="max-width:640px; margin:0; padding:15px; background:rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border-radius:6px;">
    <strong>How it works.</strong> Unraid Themer injects the selected preset's stylesheet into every page (via a <code>Buttons</code> loader page), plus a small deferred script for shadow-DOM tweaks and Docker "update available" badges.<br/><br/>
    <strong>Presets</strong> are CSS files in <code>/boot/config/plugins/unraid.themer/presets/</code> — drop your own <code>&lt;name&gt;.css</code> there to add one.<br/><br/>
    Explore Unraid's variables in <a href="/webGui/styles/themes/white.css" target="_blank">white.css</a> / <a href="/webGui/styles/themes/black.css" target="_blank">black.css</a>. Semantic status colors (disk health, array state) are intentionally left untouched by all presets.
  </span>
</form>
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/UnraidThemerIcons.page">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[Menu="Utilities"
Title="Themer Icons"
Icon="picture-o"
---
<?php
/* Unraid Themer — per-icon overrides (Settings → Utilities → Unraid Themer → Custom Icons).
 * Lists every themeable icon slot and lets the user assign a custom icon per slot:
 * a bundled Lucide name, a raw https SVG URL, or pasted <svg> markup. The chosen
 * icons are validated, stored on flash, and compiled into overrides.css, which the
 * loader injects AFTER the icon set — so a single swap wins even with set = Default.
 */
require_once "$docroot/plugins/dynamix/include/Wrappers.php";

$name    = "unraid.themer";
$flash   = "/boot/config/plugins/$name";
$webroot = "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$name";
$weburl  = "/plugins/$name";
$ov_dir_f = "$flash/overrides";       // flash: custom SVGs (persist)
$ov_dir_w = "$webroot/overrides";     // webroot: served copies
$ov_json  = "$flash/overrides.json";  // slot -> {src}
$ov_css_f = "$flash/overrides.css";
$ov_css_w = "$webroot/overrides.css";
$msg = "";

/* The themeable icon slots. `sel` = CSS selectors the override targets (must match
 * the icon-set stylesheet). `def` = bundled Lucide stem shown as the reference. */
$REG = [
    'System' => [
        'performance'    => ['Dashboard / Tower header', ['.icon-performance'], 'gauge'],
        'motherboard'    => ['Motherboard',              ['.icon-motherboard'], 'circuit-board'],
        'cpu'            => ['Processor',                ['.icon-cpu'], 'cpu'],
        'ram'            => ['Memory',                   ['.icon-ram'], 'memory-stick'],
        'ethernet'       => ['Network',                  ['.icon-ethernet'], 'ethernet-port'],
        'ups'            => ['UPS',                      ['.icon-ups'], 'battery-charging'],
        'fan'            => ['Fan',                      ['.icon-fan'], 'fan'],
        'docker'         => ['Docker',                   ['.icon-docker'], 'container'],
        'virtualization' => ['Virtual Machines',         ['.icon-virtualization'], 'monitor'],
        'folder'         => ['Shares',                   ['.icon-folder'], 'folder'],
        'users'          => ['Users',                    ['.icon-users'], 'users'],
        'user'           => ['User',                     ['.icon-user'], 'user'],
        'disks'          => ['Array / Disks',            ['.icon-disks', '.icon-disk'], 'hard-drive'],
        'disc'           => ['Disc',                     ['.icon-disc'], 'disc'],
        'health'         => ['Health',                   ['.icon-health'], 'activity'],
        'hardware'       => ['Hardware / System',        ['.icon-hardware'], 'server'],
    ],
    'Actions' => [
        'play'      => ['Start',              ['.fa-play'], 'play'],
        'stop'      => ['Stop',               ['.fa-stop'], 'square'],
        'pause'     => ['Pause',              ['.fa-pause'], 'pause'],
        'restart'   => ['Restart / Refresh',  ['.fa-refresh', '.fa-rotate-right'], 'refresh-cw'],
        'power'     => ['Power off',          ['.fa-power-off'], 'power'],
        'settings'  => ['Settings (cog)',     ['.fa-cog', '.fa-gear'], 'settings'],
        'trash'     => ['Remove (trash)',     ['.fa-trash', '.fa-trash-o'], 'trash-2'],
        'terminal'  => ['Console',            ['.fa-terminal'], 'terminal'],
        'download'  => ['Download',           ['.fa-download'], 'download'],
        'globe'     => ['WebUI / Project',    ['.fa-globe'], 'globe'],
        'wrench'    => ['Edit (wrench)',      ['.fa-wrench'], 'wrench'],
        'support'   => ['Support',            ['.fa-life-ring', '.fa-support'], 'life-buoy'],
        'logs'      => ['Logs (list)',        ['.fa-align-justify', '.fa-list', '.fa-list-ul'], 'list'],
        'info'      => ['More info',          ['.fa-info-circle', '.fa-info'], 'info'],
        'warning'   => ['Warning',            ['.fa-exclamation-triangle', '.fa-warning'], 'triangle-alert'],
        'pencil'    => ['Edit (pencil)',      ['.fa-pencil', '.fa-edit', '.fa-pencil-square-o'], 'square-pen'],
        'chevup'    => ['Chevron up',         ['.fa-chevron-up'], 'chevron-up'],
        'chevdown'  => ['Chevron down',       ['.fa-chevron-down'], 'chevron-down'],
        'menu'      => ['Menu (bars)',        ['.fa-bars', '.fa-navicon'], 'menu'],
    ],
];
// flat key -> entry, for lookups during save/CSS generation
$FLAT = [];
foreach ($REG as $cat => $slots) foreach ($slots as $k => $e) $FLAT[$k] = $e;

// bundled Lucide SVG stems (flat folder) — plain names resolve to these
$bundled = [];
foreach (glob("$webroot/icons/svg/*.svg") as $s) $bundled[] = basename($s, '.svg');
sort($bundled);
$have_bundled = array_flip($bundled);

// The visual picker offers every bundled set. Lucide values are the plain stem;
// the alternative sets use a "set/name" value (e.g. "tabler/cpu"). $all_values
// feeds the autocomplete + live preview; $picker_groups feeds the grid.
$set_labels = ['tabler' => 'Tabler', 'phosphor' => 'Phosphor', 'heroicons' => 'Heroicons',
               'iconoir' => 'Iconoir', 'remix' => 'Remix', 'bootstrap' => 'Bootstrap',
               'carbon' => 'Carbon', 'material' => 'Material Symbols', 'spongebob' => 'SpongeBob'];
$picker_groups = ['Lucide' => array_map(fn($n) => [$n, $n, "$weburl/icons/svg/$n.svg"], $bundled)];
foreach (glob("$webroot/icons/svg/*", GLOB_ONLYDIR) as $dirpath) {
    $dir = basename($dirpath);
    $label = $set_labels[$dir] ?? ucfirst($dir);
    $items = [];
    foreach (glob("$dirpath/*.svg") as $s) {
        $n = basename($s, '.svg');
        $items[$n] = ["$dir/$n", $n, "$weburl/icons/svg/$dir/$n.svg"];
    }
    ksort($items);
    if ($items) $picker_groups[$label] = array_values($items);
}
$all_values = [];
foreach ($picker_groups as $items) foreach ($items as $it) $all_values[] = $it[0];

/* Validate an SVG before it is ever written to disk. Returns [clean, error]. */
function themer_sanitize_svg($svg) {
    $svg = (string) $svg;
    if (trim($svg) === '')            return ["", "empty or download failed"];
    if (strlen($svg) > 64 * 1024)     return ["", "too large (>64 KB)"];
    if (!preg_match('/<svg[\s>]/i', $svg)) return ["", "not an <svg> document"];
    $blocked = [
        '/<\s*script/i'                                          => "a <script> tag",
        '/<\s*(foreignObject|iframe|image|use|animate|set)\b/i'  => "an embedded/external element",
        '/\son\w+\s*=/i'                                         => "an inline event handler",
        '/javascript\s*:/i'                                      => "a javascript: URI",
        '/(?:href|xlink:href)\s*=\s*[\'"]?\s*(?:https?:|\/\/|data:)/i' => "an external/data href",
        '/<!ENTITY|<!DOCTYPE/i'                                  => "an XML entity/doctype",
    ];
    foreach ($blocked as $re => $why) if (preg_match($re, $svg)) return ["", "contains $why"];
    return [$svg, ""];
}

/* Resolve one slot's raw input to a served icon URL, saving a custom SVG if needed.
 * Returns [targetUrl, error]. Empty input => ["", ""] (no override). */
function themer_resolve_icon($key, $src, $ctx) {
    extract($ctx); // $webroot, $weburl, $ov_dir_f, $ov_dir_w, $have_bundled
    $src = trim($src);
    if ($src === '') return ["", ""];

    // (0) an uploaded custom SVG already saved for this slot
    if ($src === 'upload') {
        return is_file("$ov_dir_w/$key.svg") ? ["$weburl/overrides/$key.svg", ""] : ["", "uploaded file missing"];
    }

    // (a) pasted <svg> markup
    if (stripos($src, '<svg') !== false) {
        [$clean, $err] = themer_sanitize_svg($src);
        if ($err) return ["", $err];
        @mkdir($ov_dir_f, 0755, true); @mkdir($ov_dir_w, 0755, true);
        file_put_contents("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg", $clean);
        @copy("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg", "$ov_dir_w/$key.svg");
        return ["$weburl/overrides/$key.svg", ""];
    }
    // (b) https URL to an SVG
    if (preg_match('#^https://[^\s\'"<>]+$#i', $src)) {
        $raw = shell_exec("curl -fsSL --max-time 20 --max-filesize 65536 " . escapeshellarg($src) . " 2>/dev/null");
        [$clean, $err] = themer_sanitize_svg($raw);
        if ($err) return ["", $err];
        @mkdir($ov_dir_f, 0755, true); @mkdir($ov_dir_w, 0755, true);
        file_put_contents("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg", $clean);
        @copy("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg", "$ov_dir_w/$key.svg");
        return ["$weburl/overrides/$key.svg", ""];
    }
    // (c) a bundled icon from an alternative set: "set/name" (e.g. "tabler/cpu").
    // The strict pattern (one segment / one segment, no dots) + is_file guards
    // against path traversal.
    if (preg_match('#^[a-z0-9-]+/[a-z0-9-]+$#', strtolower($src))
        && is_file("$webroot/icons/svg/" . strtolower($src) . ".svg")) {
        return ["$weburl/icons/svg/" . strtolower($src) . ".svg", ""];
    }
    // (d) a bundled Lucide stem (plain name)
    $stem = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9_-]/', '', strtolower($src));
    if ($stem !== '' && isset($have_bundled[$stem])) {
        return ["$weburl/icons/svg/$stem.svg", ""];
    }
    return ["", "not a bundled name, https URL or <svg> markup"];
}

/* (Re)compile overrides.css from the stored slot->src map. */
function themer_build_overrides_css($map, $FLAT, $ctx) {
    extract($ctx);
    $blocks = [];
    foreach ($map as $key => $src) {
        if (!isset($FLAT[$key])) continue;
        [$target, $err] = themer_resolve_icon($key, $src, $ctx);
        if ($err || $target === '') continue;
        $sel = implode(",\n", array_map(fn($s) => "$s::before", $FLAT[$key][1]));
        $blocks[] = "$sel {\n"
            . "  content: \"\" !important;\n"
            . "  -webkit-mask: url('$target') center / contain no-repeat;\n"
            . "  mask: url('$target') center / contain no-repeat;\n"
            . "  background-color: currentColor;\n"
            . "  display: inline-block; width: 1em; height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.125em;\n"
            . "}";
    }
    $css = "/* Unraid Themer — per-icon overrides (generated). */\n" . implode("\n", $blocks) . "\n";
    file_put_contents($ov_css_f, $css);
    @copy($ov_css_f, $ov_css_w);
}

$ctx = compact('webroot', 'weburl', 'ov_dir_f', 'ov_dir_w', 'have_bundled', 'ov_css_f', 'ov_css_w');

// read current override map
$map = file_exists($ov_json) ? (json_decode(file_get_contents($ov_json), true) ?: []) : [];

// --- SAVE all slots ---
if ($_POST && isset($_POST['SAVE_ICONS'])) {
    $newmap = [];
    $errs = [];
    foreach ($FLAT as $key => $e) {
        // an uploaded SVG file for this slot wins over the text field
        $up = $_FILES["up_$key"] ?? null;
        if ($up && !empty($up['tmp_name']) && is_uploaded_file($up['tmp_name'])) {
            [$clean, $err] = themer_sanitize_svg(file_get_contents($up['tmp_name']));
            if ($err) { $errs[] = "{$e[0]}: $err"; continue; }
            @mkdir($ov_dir_f, 0755, true); @mkdir($ov_dir_w, 0755, true);
            file_put_contents("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg", $clean);
            @copy("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg", "$ov_dir_w/$key.svg");
            $newmap[$key] = 'upload';
            continue;
        }
        $src = trim($_POST["ov_$key"] ?? '');
        if ($src === '') { @unlink("$ov_dir_f/$key.svg"); @unlink("$ov_dir_w/$key.svg"); continue; }
        [$target, $err] = themer_resolve_icon($key, $src, $ctx);
        if ($err) { $errs[] = "{$e[0]}: $err"; continue; }
        $newmap[$key] = $src;
    }
    $map = $newmap;
    file_put_contents($ov_json, json_encode($map, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT));
    themer_build_overrides_css($map, $FLAT, $ctx);
    $msg = $errs
        ? "Saved. Skipped: " . implode("; ", $errs) . "."
        : "Icons saved. Reload the browser (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+R) to see changes.";
}

// --- RESET all ---
if ($_POST && isset($_POST['RESET_ICONS'])) {
    foreach (glob("$ov_dir_f/*.svg") as $f) @unlink($f);
    foreach (glob("$ov_dir_w/*.svg") as $f) @unlink($f);
    @unlink($ov_json);
    file_put_contents($ov_css_f, "/* Unraid Themer — per-icon overrides (generated). */\n");
    @copy($ov_css_f, $ov_css_w);
    $map = [];
    $msg = "All custom icons cleared.";
}

// preview helper: a masked span using the given served SVG url
function themer_prev($url, $title = '') {
    if ($url === '') return "<span style='display:inline-block;width:22px;height:22px;opacity:.35;text-align:center;'>&mdash;</span>";
    $u = htmlspecialchars($url);
    return "<span title='" . htmlspecialchars($title) . "' style='display:inline-block;width:22px;height:22px;"
        . "-webkit-mask:url(\"$u\") center/contain no-repeat;mask:url(\"$u\") center/contain no-repeat;"
        . "background-color:currentColor;vertical-align:middle;'></span>";
}
?>

<style>
  #ut-icons { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; max-width: 900px; }
  #ut-icons th, #ut-icons td { padding: 6px 10px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.18); text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; }
  #ut-icons th { border-top: none; font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; opacity: .7; }
  #ut-icons tr.ut-cat td { padding-top: 16px; font-weight: 700; opacity: .85; border-top: none; }
  #ut-icons input[type=text] { width: 100%; min-width: 200px; }
  #ut-icons .ut-desc { white-space: nowrap; }
  #ut-icons .ut-cell { display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }
  #ut-icons .ut-pick { flex: none; width: 32px; height: 30px; padding: 0; cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background: rgba(128,128,128,0.14) !important; border: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.4) !important;
    border-radius: 6px !important; box-shadow: none !important; color: var(--text-color, #e6e6e6) !important; }
  #ut-icons .ut-pick:hover { background: rgba(128,128,128,0.26) !important; }
  #ut-icons .ut-pick span { width: 16px; height: 16px; display: inline-block; background-color: currentColor;
    -webkit-mask: url('<?= $weburl ?>/icons/svg/list.svg') center/contain no-repeat; mask: url('<?= $weburl ?>/icons/svg/list.svg') center/contain no-repeat; }
  #ut-icons .ut-up span { -webkit-mask-image: url('<?= $weburl ?>/icons/svg/upload.svg'); mask-image: url('<?= $weburl ?>/icons/svg/upload.svg'); }

  /* visual icon picker (modal grid) */
  #ut-picker-backdrop { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.55); z-index: 9998; }
  #ut-picker { display: none; position: fixed; z-index: 9999; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%,-50%);
    width: min(680px, 94vw); max-height: 80vh; background: var(--background-color, #1c1f26); color: var(--text-color, #e6e6e6);
    border: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.4); border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.5); display: none; flex-direction: column; }
  #ut-picker.open { display: flex; }
  #ut-picker-head { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.25); }
  #ut-picker-head input { flex: 1; }
  #ut-picker-head .ut-x { flex: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px 10px; }
  #ut-picker-grid { overflow-y: auto; padding: 10px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(64px, 1fr)); gap: 6px; }
  .ut-pick-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 4px; padding: 8px 4px; cursor: pointer;
    background: transparent; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 8px; color: inherit; }
  .ut-pick-item:hover { border-color: rgba(128,128,128,0.4); background: rgba(128,128,128,0.12); }
  .ut-pick-item span.ico { width: 24px; height: 24px; background-color: currentColor;
    -webkit-mask-position: center; mask-position: center; -webkit-mask-size: contain; mask-size: contain; -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat; mask-repeat: no-repeat; }
  .ut-pick-item small { font-size: 10px; opacity: .7; max-width: 60px; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .ut-pick-group { grid-column: 1 / -1; font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em;
    opacity: .6; padding: 10px 4px 2px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.18); }
  .ut-pick-group:first-child { border-top: none; padding-top: 2px; }
</style>

<div markdown="1">
<?php if ($msg): ?>
<span class="green"><?= htmlspecialchars($msg) ?></span>
<?php endif; ?>

<a href="/Settings/UnraidThemer">&larr; Back to Unraid Themer</a>

Assign a custom icon to any slot below. Leave a field empty to keep the icon-set default.
Use the **grid button** to pick from all bundled sets (Lucide, Tabler, Phosphor, Heroicons,
Iconoir, Remix, Bootstrap, Carbon, Material Symbols), the **upload button** to upload your own
**SVG file**, or type into the field: a **bundled name** (e.g. `cpu` or `tabler/cpu`), a raw **https SVG URL**
(e.g. from [lucide.dev](https://lucide.dev) or [tabler.io/icons](https://tabler.io/icons)), or
pasted **`<svg>…</svg>`** markup. Custom SVGs are validated (no scripts/handlers/external refs)
and tinted with the theme color, so single-color line icons work best.
</div>

<form method="POST" action="/Settings/UnraidThemerIcons" autocomplete="off" enctype="multipart/form-data">
<datalist id="ut-bundled">
  <?php foreach ($all_values as $b): ?><option value="<?= htmlspecialchars($b) ?>"><?php endforeach; ?>
</datalist>

<table id="ut-icons">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Icon</th><th>Set&nbsp;icon</th><th>Yours</th><th>Custom (name, https URL or &lt;svg&gt;)</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  <?php foreach ($REG as $cat => $slots): ?>
    <tr class="ut-cat"><td colspan="4"><?= htmlspecialchars($cat) ?></td></tr>
    <?php foreach ($slots as $key => $e):
        [$label, $sel, $def] = $e;
        $ref_url = isset($have_bundled[$def]) ? "$weburl/icons/svg/$def.svg" : "";
        $src = $map[$key] ?? '';
        [$own_url] = $src !== '' ? themer_resolve_icon($key, $src, $ctx) : ['', ''];
    ?>
    <tr>
      <td class="ut-desc"><?= htmlspecialchars($label) ?></td>
      <td><?= themer_prev($ref_url, $def) ?></td>
      <td class="ut-own" data-key="<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>"><?= themer_prev($own_url, $src) ?></td>
      <td><div class="ut-cell">
        <button type="button" class="ut-pick" title="Pick from the icon grid" onclick="utOpenPicker('<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>')"><span></span></button>
        <button type="button" class="ut-pick ut-up" title="Upload an SVG file" onclick="document.getElementById('up_<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>').click()"><span></span></button>
        <input type="file" id="up_<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>" name="up_<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>" accept=".svg,image/svg+xml" style="display:none" onchange="utUploadPrev(this,'<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>')">
        <input type="text" name="ov_<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>" list="ut-bundled"
               value="<?= htmlspecialchars($src) ?>" spellcheck="false"
               placeholder="<?= htmlspecialchars($def) ?>"
               oninput="utIconPrev(this)" data-key="<?= htmlspecialchars($key) ?>">
      </div></td>
    </tr>
    <?php endforeach; ?>
  <?php endforeach; ?>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p style="margin-top:16px;">
  <input type="submit" name="SAVE_ICONS" value="_(Apply)_">
  <input type="submit" name="RESET_ICONS" value="Reset all" onclick="return confirm('Clear all custom icons?')">
  <input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</p>
</form>

<!-- visual icon picker: a searchable grid of the bundled Lucide icons -->
<div id="ut-picker-backdrop" onclick="utClosePicker()"></div>
<div id="ut-picker" role="dialog" aria-label="Pick an icon" data-weburl="<?= htmlspecialchars($weburl) ?>" data-values="<?= htmlspecialchars(json_encode($all_values)) ?>">
  <div id="ut-picker-head">
    <input type="text" id="ut-picker-search" placeholder="Search icons…" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" oninput="utPickerFilter()">
    <button type="button" class="ut-x" onclick="utClosePicker()">&times;</button>
  </div>
  <div id="ut-picker-grid">
    <?php foreach ($picker_groups as $glabel => $items): ?>
    <div class="ut-pick-group" data-group="<?= htmlspecialchars(strtolower($glabel)) ?>"><?= htmlspecialchars($glabel) ?></div>
    <?php foreach ($items as [$val, $name, $url]): $v = htmlspecialchars($val); $nm = htmlspecialchars($name); ?>
    <button type="button" class="ut-pick-item" data-search="<?= htmlspecialchars(strtolower($name . ' ' . $glabel . ' ' . $val)) ?>" title="<?= $v ?>" onclick="utPick('<?= $v ?>')">
      <span class="ico" style="-webkit-mask-image:url('<?= $url ?>');mask-image:url('<?= $url ?>');"></span>
      <small><?= $nm ?></small>
    </button>
    <?php endforeach; ?>
    <?php endforeach; ?>
  </div>
</div>

<script defer src="/plugins/unraid.themer/js/themer-icons.js?v=<?= @filemtime("$webroot/js/themer-icons.js") ?>"></script>
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/UnraidThemerLoader.page">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[Menu="Buttons:100"
Link="nav-user"
---
<?php
/* Unraid Themer — global loader.
 * Runs in <head> on every page (Menu="Buttons"). Injects the active preset
 * stylesheet, optional user overrides, and the runtime JS — only when enabled.
 *
 * IMPORTANT: this executes in the page's GLOBAL PHP scope, so it must NOT leak
 * variables (e.g. $name collides with Unraid's device/share name and breaks
 * those pages). Everything is wrapped in an immediately-invoked closure.
 */
(function () {
    global $docroot;
    require_once "$docroot/plugins/dynamix/include/Wrappers.php";

    $name    = "unraid.themer";
    $webroot = "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$name";
    $weburl  = "/plugins/$name";

    $cfg = parse_plugin_cfg($name);
    if (($cfg['SERVICE'] ?? "disabled") !== "enabled") return;

    // selected preset (sanitised to a safe filename stem)
    $preset = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/', '', $cfg['PRESET'] ?? 'bebamu');

    // 1) preset stylesheet
    if ($preset !== '' && $preset !== 'none') {
        $preset_file = "$webroot/presets/$preset.css";
        if (file_exists($preset_file)) {
            $v = filemtime($preset_file);
            echo "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"$weburl/presets/$preset.css?v=$v\">\n";
        }
    }

    // 1b) sidebar-layout polish (Azure/Gray header band + nav accent); preset-agnostic
    $layout = "$webroot/layout.css";
    if (file_exists($layout)) {
        $v = filemtime($layout);
        echo "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"$weburl/layout.css?v=$v\">\n";
    }

    // 2) icon set (replaces Unraid's UI glyphs; loaded after the preset)
    $iconset = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/', '', $cfg['ICONSET'] ?? 'default');
    if ($iconset !== '' && $iconset !== 'default') {
        $icss = "$webroot/icons/$iconset.css";
        if (file_exists($icss)) {
            $v = filemtime($icss);
            echo "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"$weburl/icons/$iconset.css?v=$v\">\n";
        }
    }

    // 3) per-icon overrides (loaded AFTER the icon set so single-icon swaps win,
    //    and work even when the icon set is "default")
    $ovcss = "$webroot/overrides.css";
    if (file_exists($ovcss) && trim(file_get_contents($ovcss)) !== '') {
        $v = filemtime($ovcss);
        echo "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"$weburl/overrides.css?v=$v\">\n";
    }

    // 4) user custom overrides (loaded AFTER the preset so they win)
    $override = "$webroot/custom.css";
    if (file_exists($override) && trim(file_get_contents($override)) !== '') {
        $v = filemtime($override);
        echo "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"$weburl/custom.css?v=$v\">\n";
    }

    // 3) runtime JS (shadow-DOM tweaks, update badges) — deferred, same-origin (CSP-safe)
    $js = "$webroot/js/themer.js";
    if (file_exists($js)) {
        $v = filemtime($js);
        echo "<script defer src=\"$weburl/js/themer.js?v=$v\"></script>\n";
    }
})();
?>
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid.themer/default.cfg">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[SERVICE="disabled"
PRESET="bebamu"
